<title>UK: UK Oct non-EU trade deficit 424 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Oct non-EU trade deficit 424 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released following seasonally adjusted UK non-EU Trade data-</p>
<p>    UK TRADE NON-EU (in million stg)    OCT	SEPT   (PREL SEPT)</p>
<p>    Trade balance			 -424     -805     (-851)</p>
<p>    Exports (FOB)			 6,272    5,905   (5,920)</p>
<p>    Imports (FOB)			 6,696    6,710   (6,771)</p>
<p>    Oil exports			     276	260     (260)</p>
<p>    Oil imports			     410	372     (371)</p>
<p>    Trade balance 3m ending	   -1,764     n/a  (-2,167)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast 800 million stg deficit.</p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 142.1    146.5   (147.6)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 139.4    135.2   (135.6)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)   2.0%    4.0%    (4.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps)  10.0%   12.0%   (13.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)   1.0%    2.0%    (2.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps)  10.0%    9.5%    (9.5%)</p>
<p>TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Balance (million stg)		-331    -699     (-743)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)   0.5%    1.5%    (2.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)   1.0%    1.5%    (1.5%)</p>
<p>The ONS said the provisional estimates of volume excluding oil and erratics show exports up three percent to a record monthly level and imports down three percent.</p>
</text>
